WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.107
We are Team Vibecoders.

00:00:02.107 --> 00:00:07.450
This is TidePlan, a working microloan cash-flow planning prototype.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:11.850
A missed date is not always a missing ability to repay.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:18.058
We help lenders and borrowers agree on when repayment is genuinely affordable.

00:00:18.058 --> 00:00:22.380
This demo uses synthetic data and moves no real money.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.566
We start with Asha, a smallholder farmer.

00:00:26.566 --> 00:00:29.115
Her history shows seasonal income.

00:00:29.115 --> 00:00:34.214
A fixed six-month repayment breaches her protected cash buffer twice.

00:00:34.214 --> 00:00:44.483
TidePlan aligns the same eighteen-thousand-rupee obligation to conservative monthly capacity, keeping every month above her selected buffer.

00:00:45.684 --> 00:00:52.471
In Plan Studio, the buffer protects essentials and existing debt before repayment is allocated.

00:00:52.471 --> 00:00:59.401
Change the buffer or apply an income shock, and compare fixed and aligned schedules immediately.

00:00:59.401 --> 00:01:07.404
The model uses transparent TypeScript rules and a conservative income haircut, not an unexplained credit score.

00:01:08.604 --> 00:01:14.463
At a sixty-percent shock, there is not enough safe capacity to settle the loan.

00:01:14.463 --> 00:01:19.062
TidePlan shows the unscheduled balance and disables approval.

00:01:19.062 --> 00:01:23.735
That is intentional: a flexible schedule cannot create income.

00:01:23.735 --> 00:01:29.076
It signals human review, support, or separately assessed restructuring.

00:01:30.276 --> 00:01:32.834
We return to a manageable scenario.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:41.313
The lender approves the exact payments, then the borrower sees the same monthly schedule and explicitly accepts it.

00:01:41.313 --> 00:01:47.014
Change the data, safety buffer, or shock, and the approval no longer matches.

00:01:47.014 --> 00:01:51.108
What-if analysis never silently changes an agreed plan.

00:01:52.308 --> 00:01:57.985
The Trust Ledger records approval and consent as a linked SHA-256 history.

00:01:57.985 --> 00:02:03.586
We verify the chain, test a tampered copy, and export decision evidence.

00:02:03.586 --> 00:02:10.261
A simulated reserve can support an approved shock scenario, but it transfers no funds.

00:02:10.261 --> 00:02:16.475
Blockchain contracts are future integration blueprints, not live infrastructure.

00:02:17.676 --> 00:02:22.304
React and TypeScript power the interface and cash-flow engine.

00:02:22.304 --> 00:02:30.814
Recharts makes the alternatives visible, Papa Parse validates local CSV data, and GitHub Pages hosts the product.

00:02:30.814 --> 00:02:39.772
TidePlan is built for a responsible pilot: measure affordability, recovery, forecast error, and borrower cost together.

00:02:39.772 --> 00:02:43.355
Team Vibecoders: repayment in rhythm with life.

